# shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS v4

Project-specific companion to cursor-designer frontend rules. Stack defaults follow shadcn’s theme/templates (`components.json`: `radix-nova`, `baseColor: neutral`, CSS variables).

## Primitives first

- Build UI from `@/components/ui/*` (Button, Dialog, Sheet, Sidebar, Form controls, etc.).
- Shared kits: `@/components/table` for DataTable; `@/components/layout` for app chrome.
- Prefer composing primitives over custom one-off controls. If a shadcn component is missing, add it via CLI before hand-rolling.

## Styling

- **Tailwind v4** only — no `tailwind.config.js`. Tokens live in `src/styles.css` (`:root` / `.dark` + `@theme inline`).
- Prefer semantic utility classes mapped from CSS vars: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `bg-primary-soft`, `border-border`, `ring-ring`, `rounded-lg`, etc.
- Do **not** hardcode hex/oklch in feature components when a token covers the role (`design/tokens/colors.md`).
- Spacing: Tailwind default scale (`gap-4`, `p-6`, …) per `design/tokens/spacing.md`. Avoid arbitrary values (`p-[13px]`) unless documented as an exception.
- Icons: **Lucide** (`lucide-react`), consistent size (`size-4` in dense chrome).

## Variants and hierarchy

- Buttons: use shadcn `variant` / `size` (`default`, `outline`, `ghost`, `destructive`, …). One primary action per region.
- Destructive actions: `variant="destructive"` + confirm pattern already used in classrooms (dialog title + clear consequence).
- Dense LMS chrome: prefer `text-sm`; page titles `text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight` (`design/tokens/typography.md`).

## Dark mode

- Theme uses class `.dark` (`@custom-variant dark`). Use semantic tokens so light/dark stay in sync — do not invent separate color branches in components.

## Anti-patterns

- Do not add a second component library or CSS framework.
- Do not restyle shadcn primitives with large one-off class dumps when a variant or token extension would do.
- Do not replace Radix-backed dialogs/menus/sheets with custom modals that lack focus trap / Escape / return focus.
